   "body": "<p><i lang=\"es\">En tanto que</i> means “so long as.” The sentence runs on until <i lang=\"es\">coged</i>: so long as the color shows, and so long as the wind moves the hair, gather the fruit. <i lang=\"es\">Se muestra</i> is “shows,” from <i lang=\"es\">mostrar</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Color</i> is feminine here, <i lang=\"es\">la color</i>, as it often was in the Spanish of the period. <i lang=\"es\">Gesto</i> is the face. <i lang=\"es\">Vuestro</i> agrees with it.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">Mirar</i> here is the gaze, a noun. <i lang=\"es\">Ardiente</i> is “burning,” and <i lang=\"es\">honesto</i> is “modest” (Academy, <i lang=\"es\">honesto</i>, 2: <i lang=\"es\">recatado, pudoroso</i>). Both agree with <i lang=\"es\">mirar</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Serena</i> is the present of <i lang=\"es\">serenar</i>, “calms.” The gaze, with a clear light, calms the storm.</p>"
