   "title": "The white day",
   "body": "<p><i lang=\"es\">Cerrar podrá mis ojos la postrera sombra, que me llevare el blanco dia.</i> <i lang=\"es\">Cerrar</i> is the infinitive of the verb “to close.” <i lang=\"es\">Podrá</i> is the future of <i lang=\"es\">poder</i>, and the subject is <i lang=\"es\">la postrera sombra</i>, the last shadow. <i lang=\"es\">Llevare</i> is the future subjunctive of <i lang=\"es\">llevar</i>. Its subject is <i lang=\"es\">que</i>, which stands for the shadow, and its object is <i lang=\"es\">el blanco dia</i>: the shadow that will take the white day from me. The print writes no accent on <i lang=\"es\">llevare</i> or on <i lang=\"es\">dia</i>.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">Y podrá desatar esta alma mia hora, á su afan ansioso lisonjera.</i> <i lang=\"es\">Desatar</i> is “to untie.” <i lang=\"es\">Hora</i> is the subject, an hour, and <i lang=\"es\">lisonjera</i> agrees with it: the hour flatters. <i lang=\"es\">Afan</i> is a longing, and the print writes it with no accent. The comma in <i lang=\"es\">Hora ,</i> stands a space away from the word, as this print sets it. <i lang=\"es\">Mia</i> agrees with <i lang=\"es\">alma</i>, and it too has no accent.</p>"
