   "body": "<p><i lang=\"es\">Con diez cañones por banda.</i> <i lang=\"es\">Con</i>, <i lang=\"es\">diez</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ca</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ño</i>, <i lang=\"es\">nes</i>, <i lang=\"es\">por</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ban</i>, <i lang=\"es\">da</i>. Eight. <i lang=\"es\">Banda</i> is stressed on <i lang=\"es\">ban</i>.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">Viento en popa, á toda vela.</i> <i lang=\"es\">Vien</i>, <i lang=\"es\">toen</i>, <i lang=\"es\">po</i>, <i lang=\"es\">paá</i>, <i lang=\"es\">to</i>, <i lang=\"es\">da</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ve</i>, <i lang=\"es\">la</i>. The <i lang=\"es\">o</i> of <i lang=\"es\">viento</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">en</i>. The <i lang=\"es\">a</i> of <i lang=\"es\">popa</i> joins the preposition <i lang=\"es\">á</i>. That preposition is unstressed. The written accent marks the word. Eight. The stress falls on <i lang=\"es\">ve</i>.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">No corta el mar sino vuela.</i> <i lang=\"es\">No</i>, <i lang=\"es\">cor</i>, <i lang=\"es\">tael</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mar</i>, <i lang=\"es\">si</i>, <i lang=\"es\">no</i>, <i lang=\"es\">vue</i>, <i lang=\"es\">la</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Corta</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">el</i>. The vowels <i lang=\"es\">u</i> and <i lang=\"es\">e</i> in <i lang=\"es\">vuela</i> are one syllable. Eight.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">Un velero bergantin.</i> <i lang=\"es\">Un</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ve</i>, <i lang=\"es\">le</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ro</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ber</i>, <i lang=\"es\">gan</i>, <i lang=\"es\">tin</i>. Seven syllables are written. The stress is on <i lang=\"es\">tin</i>, so the line counts one more. Eight. The print writes no accent. <i lang=\"es\">Confin</i> is the same kind of ending: <i lang=\"es\">Del</i>, <i lang=\"es\">u</i>, <i lang=\"es\">noal</i>, <i lang=\"es\">o</i>, <i lang=\"es\">tro</i>, <i lang=\"es\">con</i>, <i lang=\"es\">fin</i>. The <i lang=\"es\">o</i> of <i lang=\"es\">uno</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">al</i>. Seven are written, and the stress on <i lang=\"es\">fin</i> adds one. The rhyme of the two lines is the vowel <i lang=\"es\">i</i>.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">La luna en el mar rïela.</i> <i lang=\"es\">La</i>, <i lang=\"es\">lu</i>, <i lang=\"es\">naen</i>, <i lang=\"es\">el</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mar</i>, <i lang=\"es\">rï</i>, <i lang=\"es\">e</i>, <i lang=\"es\">la</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Luna</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">en</i>. The two dots keep <i lang=\"es\">i</i> and <i lang=\"es\">e</i> apart, so <i lang=\"es\">rïela</i> is three syllables, and the stress of that word falls on <i lang=\"es\">e</i>. Eight. If <i lang=\"es\">i</i> and <i lang=\"es\">e</i> were one syllable, the line would have seven. The count of eight rests on the diaeresis.</p><p><i lang=\"es\">Olas de plata y azul.</i> <i lang=\"es\">O</i>, <i lang=\"es\">las</i>, <i lang=\"es\">de</i>, <i lang=\"es\">pla</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ta</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ya</i>, <i lang=\"es\">zul</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Y</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">a</i>. Seven are written. <i lang=\"es\">Azul</i> is stressed on the last syllable, so the line counts eight.</p><p>The refrain keeps the same count. <i lang=\"es\">Que es mi barco mi tesoro</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">Que</i> and <i lang=\"es\">es</i>: <i lang=\"es\">Quees</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mi</i>, <i lang=\"es\">bar</i>, <i lang=\"es\">co</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mi</i>, <i lang=\"es\">te</i>, <i lang=\"es\">so</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ro</i>. Eight. <i lang=\"es\">Que es mi Dios la libertad</i> is <i lang=\"es\">Quees</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mi</i>, <i lang=\"es\">Dios</i>, <i lang=\"es\">la</i>, <i lang=\"es\">li</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ber</i>, <i lang=\"es\">tad</i>. Seven are written, and <i lang=\"es\">libertad</i> adds one. <i lang=\"es\">Mi ley la fuerza y el viento</i> joins <i lang=\"es\">y</i> and <i lang=\"es\">el</i>. In <i lang=\"es\">fuerza</i> the vowels <i lang=\"es\">u</i> and <i lang=\"es\">e</i> are one syllable, and in <i lang=\"es\">viento</i> the vowels <i lang=\"es\">i</i> and <i lang=\"es\">e</i> are one syllable. Eight. <i lang=\"es\">Mi única patria la mar</i> is eight only if <i lang=\"es\">Mi</i> joins the stressed <i lang=\"es\">ú</i>: <i lang=\"es\">Miú</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ni</i>, <i lang=\"es\">ca</i>, <i lang=\"es\">pa</i>, <i lang=\"es\">tria</i>, <i lang=\"es\">la</i>, <i lang=\"es\">mar</i>. <i lang=\"es\">Ia</i> in <i lang=\"es\">patria</i> is a diphthong. Seven are written, and <i lang=\"es\">mar</i> adds one. The count of that one line rests on the join, which the other lines of the refrain allow, and on the rule that an unstressed weak vowel can join the vowel beside it (Robles Dégano, <i>Ortología clásica</i>, §99, page 86).</p>"
